Description: Tools for preparing, validating and comparing ecological
    interaction networks across space and time. The package supports
    weighted, binary, directed, undirected, unipartite and multipartite
    networks, and provides methods to classify species turnover,
    interaction persistence, gain, loss and rewiring, quantify changes in
    interaction strength, and summarize link-change patterns between
    networks.
